{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Autonomous secrets-rotation attempt — OUTCOME: nothing rotated (all deferred). No AWS mutation performed.\n\nPer operator authorization to rotate ONLY secrets that are (a) mintable by me AND (b) non-breaking/self-healing, with `terraform apply` still forbidden. I enumerated every SecureString from `local.rebar_secret_params` (infra/terraform/ssm.tf) plus the auth `/auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET`, verified `ssm:PutParameter` is allowed for my identity (`arn:aws:iam::896586841071:user/joe_frontier`, us-east-1), and classified each. **After investigation, ZERO secrets qualify as autonomous-rotatable — every candidate has a hard blocker. I ran no `put-parameter` and no `terraform apply`.**\n\n### Classification table\n\n**AUTONOMOUS-ROTATABLE — (none)**\nOn investigation, the two nominally \"random/mintable\" candidates both failed the non-breaking/self-healing test (details below). No secret was rotated.\n\n**COORDINATION-SENSITIVE — DEFER (mintable, but rotation breaks a chain this workflow / another consumer depends on)**\n| Secret | Why deferred |\n|---|---|\n| `/auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET` (SSO cookie-signing key) | **Named by the task as the autonomous example — but investigation shows it is NOT.** The key is **baked into Lambda@Edge bundles at deploy** (edge functions can't read SSM at runtime). I found **`lmn-sso-gate` + `lmn-staging-sso-gate`** (nodejs20.x, mod 2026-08-12) DEPLOYED, fronting the `modernization-navigator[-staging].solutions.navateam.com` CloudFront distributions (the Legacy-Modernization-Navigator app — a **different team/project** sharing this domain's SSO). Rotating the SSM value → auth-host signs cookies with the NEW key while those baked edge gates verify with the OLD key → **modernization-navigator production SSO breaks** until LMN redeploys its edge bundles. Not self-healing, cross-team, and outside the stated `/rebar/prod/*` scope. The runbook's \"rebar currently runs no gate instance\" is true only for rebar; LMN's gates are live. Write-only, so no true rollback either. → **DEFER to a coordinated LMN-inclusive window.** |\n| `/rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key` | Op-cert attestation signing key underpinning plan-review / completion-verifier — the gates THIS close-chain uses. DEFER (task's own default). |\n| `/rebar/prod/mcp-hmac-signing-key` | \"verdict signing\" (fetch-secrets.sh:13) — MCP gate-verdict signing chain. Rotating mid-session risks verdict-signature verification. DEFER. |\n| `/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key` | Authorship/attestation signing; also mirrored to GHA secret `REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY` — must rotate the pair together. DEFER. |\n| `/rebar/prod/opcert-origin-guard` | **terraform-GENERATED** (`random_password`), injected as an API-GW header. Can't rotate out-of-band without tf drift + header mismatch (needs an apply). DEFER. |\n| `/rebar/prod/gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key` | SSH **host** key — rotating trips `known_hosts` for every client incl. CI's SSH-to-Gerrit Verified-vote path. Not self-healing. DEFER. |\n| `/rebar/prod/gerrit-admin-password` | Mintable but must also be set on the Gerrit account (external coordination). DEFER. |\n\n**EXTERNAL-MANUAL — DEFER (third-party issued; I cannot mint)**\n`github-oauth-client-secret`, `reviewbot-tickets-pat`, `mcp-tickets-pat`, `mcp-client-pat-copilot|claude|codex`, `g2p-github-pat`, `github-*` (replication deploy key), `gerrit-bot-token`, `jira-api-token`, `anthropic-api-key`, and the `alert-endpoint` webhook URL (config value, not mintable). Each requires a human in an external console/provider.\n\n### Nothing rotated — and why that's the safe outcome\nThe task said \"default to defer\" for coordination-sensitive secrets and \"if a rotation breaks something, stop.\" My investigation caught the break **before** it happened: the one secret named as the autonomous example (cookie key) would have taken down another team's production SSO. Everything else is external, terraform-managed, or feeds the very gates/session in use. So the correct, evidence-based result is **zero autonomous rotations**.\n\n### Remaining manual steps (all deferred to the operator maintenance window)\n1. **The `value_wo` cutover `terraform apply`** (this ticket's step 1) — clobbers all 21 SecureStrings to `CHANGEME`; must be operator-supervised.\n2. **Re-seed / rotate ALL 21 real values in the SAME window** (step 2) — since the cutover resets every slot, this is mandatory regardless of any pre-rotation; any value I might have set would just be re-clobbered.\n3. **Cross-team coordination for the cookie key**: schedule the LMN edge-gate (`lmn-sso-gate` / `lmn-staging-sso-gate`) redeploy alongside any cookie-secret rotation, or `modernization-navigator` SSO breaks.\n4. **External rotations** (step 2 crown-jewels + all EXTERNAL-MANUAL secrets) in each provider console, updating every dependent system (GHA mirrors, Gerrit/Jira accounts, GitHub OAuth app, Anthropic console).\n5. **State scrub** (steps 3–4): verify `terraform state pull` shows no SecureString value; purge historical cleartext from the retained `s3://rebar-tfstate-896586841071/rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate` versions.\n\nNo secret values are recorded here or anywhere. `9350` and the rubied ticket remain OPEN (their clean-apply close is gated on this deferred cutover). Change 2389 (config-only import blocks) worktree kept intact."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788044981045312425,"uuid":"5223a712-d2e8-47a8-9114-03653219d6fe"}